diagnosis_text:
I cannot reproduce the reported outage for web1.local from host_1_1_1_1. End-to-end checks show the service and path are healthy:

- Name resolution works on host_1_1_1_1: getent hosts web1.local returns 10.200.0.4, using DNS server 10.200.0.2 as configured in resolv.conf (nsswitch set to “files dns”).
- Connectivity is good: host_1_1_1_1 can ping web_server_1 (10.200.0.4) with 0% loss and ~3 ms RTT.
- HTTP service is responsive: curl http://web1.local and http://10.200.0.4 both return HTTP 200 with ~5 ms total time, repeatedly.
- On web_server_1, Apache (apache2) is enabled and running, and netstat shows it listening on 0.0.0.0:80.
- On dns_server, named (BIND) is running and listening on 10.200.0.2:53, and the host can resolve web1.local via DNS.

Mechanistically, a dead page would require DNS failure, reachability loss, or an HTTP daemon issue; none are present now. Localization: no faulty device or interface identified; both web_server_1 and dns_server subsystems are healthy. Root cause: not reproducible at this time; the earlier symptom was likely transient (e.g., brief service restart or client-side hiccup).

Corrective fix: No change required. If the issue recurs, please capture the exact time and we will review web_server_1’s Apache logs and dns_server query logs for correlation and consider adding health checks/monitoring to catch intermittent faults. === END ===